The review-thread resolution machinery already resolved GitHub PR review
threads from ANY author — CodeRabbit, Qodo, Greptile, or a human — via
GraphQL/REST, but its "greptile" naming implied it was Greptile-specific.

- Rename .claude/scripts/greptile-resolve.sh → review-resolve.sh
- Rename .claude/rules/greptile-review-process.md → review-process.md
- De-brand skills/review + skills/shepherd (canonical) and the review-process
  rule to tool-neutral "review agent" language; Greptile kept as ONE example
- Regenerate .codex skill mirror (populateAgentSkills; in sync)
- Update all in-repo refs: lib/adapters/pr-state-adapter.js default script path,
  lib/reset.js inventory, lib/commands/setup.js scaffold list, affected tests,
  and the manual/Greptile review guides
- Greptile-the-product surfaces unchanged: greptile-review-adapter.js,
  greptile-match.js, greptile-quality-gate.yml, GREPTILE_SETUP.md framing

Full suite 4405 pass / 0 fail; eslint --max-warnings 0 clean; release check 0.1.0 = 0 blockers.

